      "side": 1,
      "message": "It might be tidier to define a new type of mkbp event: EC_MKBP_EVENT_MOTIONSENSE_FIFO_GETTING_AS_CROWDED_AS_MY_OFFICE\n(or maybe a shorter name...)\n\nThis could be followed by the number of events currently in the FIFO.  That would reduce the proposed command sequence of\n\n   EC_CMD_GET_NEXT_EVENT\n      --\u003e host event flags with MOTION_SENSOR_FIFO bit\n   EC_CMD_MOTIONSENSE (MOTIONSENSE_FIFO_INFO)\n      --\u003e FIFO count\n   EC_CMD_MOTIONSENSE (MOTIONSENSE_FIFO_READ)\n      --\u003e FIFO entries\n\nto just:\n\n   EC_CMD_GET_NEXT_EVENT\n      --\u003e MKBP motionsense event with FIFO count\n   EC_CMD_MOTIONSENSE (MOTIONSENSE_FIFO_READ)\n      --\u003e FIFO entries\n\nor you could even put FIFO entries directly in the MKBP event:\n\n   EC_CMD_GET_NEXT_EVENT\n      --\u003e MKBP motionsense event\n          (number of entries which follow)\n          (and maybe a count of entries still in the FIFO)\n          FIFO entries\n\nIf you want to get fancy, you could also add a host motionsense command to set the FIFO level at which the MKBP motionsense event would be triggered, and how many entries (if any) should be appended to the MKBP event itself.",
